    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All tests green \u2014 full suite: **58 tests, 0 failures, BUILD SUCCESS**, including the new `Cp46Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nConverted owner deletion to a soft-delete across the OfficeFloor pipeline and persistence layers:\n\n**Domain / persistence**\n- `Owner.java` \u2014 added a `deleted` boolean field (defaulting to `false`) with getter/setter, mapped to a new `deleted` column.\n- `db/{hsqldb,h2,postgres,mysql}/schema.sql` \u2014 added the `deleted` column (`DEFAULT FALSE`/`DEFAULT 0`) so a newly created owner is `false`.\n\n**API contract**\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added a read-only `deleted` boolean to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct maps it by name into every `GET`/create response.\n\n**Behavior**\n- `DeleteOwner.java` \u2014 `DELETE /api/owners/{id}` now sets `deleted = true` and `save`s the owner (retaining the row, returning 204 which is 2xx) instead of removing it; `GET` still returns the owner afterwards with `deleted: true`.\n- `RequireUniqueOwnerIdentity`, `RequireUniqueOwnerHousehold`, `AssignPossibleDuplicate` \u2014 each now skips existing owners flagged `deleted`, so a normally-blocking duplicate/identity match is allowed when the only match has been soft-deleted.\n\nThe new `Cp46Tests` cover both the flag-and-retain behavior and the deleted-owner-ignored-by-duplicate-check behavior, and the whole existing suite still passes.",
